# Caravans leaving Ridgemere and the towns, each with its own cargo and worry (Docs/Design/30-towns-and-talk.md).
# Blanks: {other}. Alternatives run in parallel.

scene em_dp_westmarch_wool
when topic=caravan kind=left region=larkfield
a : The wool carts left for {other}. Half the downs' fleeces on one road. | Wagons of hides and wool off to {other}. | The caravan took our wool to {other}. Now we wait for the coin.
b : Pray it gets there. | Smelly cargo. | Waiting's the hard part.
a : Every night. | Smells like money. | Always is.

scene em_dp_lakeside_boats
when topic=caravan kind=left region=coldwater
a : They loaded a whole boat hull on a wagon for {other}. | Smoked pike from the lake went off to {other} this morning. | The caravan to {other} took two of the boatwrights' best oars.
b : A boat on wheels. Madness. | Lucky {other}. | Best oars for the worst roads.
a : Beautiful madness. | Very lucky. | Sad but true.

scene em_dp_cinderbrook_ingots
when topic=caravan kind=left region=frosthollow
a : Ore stacked so high the wagon groaned leaving for {other}. | The ore's gone to {other}. The yard's quiet tonight. | Off goes our sweat to {other}, in lumps.
b : Heavy road ahead. | Quiet is rare here. | In lumps and for pennies.
a : Heavy and slow. | Enjoy it. | Always pennies.

scene em_dp_fenhollow_peat
when topic=caravan kind=left region=mirebridge
a : Dried peat bricks and herbs off to {other}. Our whole year. | The caravan to {other} smelled of mint and bog. | Wagons to {other}, loaded with sleep-herbs for city wolves who can't sleep.
b : Your whole year, rolling. | A fine smell. | City wolves never sleep.
a : Rolling and bumping. | Fine and strange. | Too much wine.

scene em_dp_amberford_seed
when topic=caravan kind=left region=southmeadow
a : Seed grain went to {other}. We kept the best back. | The caravan to {other} got out the gate without losing a sack. | Wagons heavy with flour left for {other}.
b : Wise. | A first. | Heavy and slow.
a : Always. | A miracle. | And dusty.

scene em_dp_accord_crossing_down
when topic=caravan kind=left region=larkfield
a : Wagons went out to {other} empty. They'll fill there. | The caravan to {other} took the mules we rented out. | Off to {other}. The market's half empty already.
b : Empty wagons, fast wagons. | Bring them back fat. | And quiet.
a : Fast and rattling. | Fat and tired. | Very quiet.

scene em_dp_saltreach_fish
when topic=caravan kind=left region=ridgemere
a : The smoked fish wagons left for {other}. Smell followed them to the gate. | Barrels of brine off to {other}. Mind the leaks. | Our salt's gone to {other}. The Sump will grumble.
b : It'll follow them all the way. | Every barrel leaks. | The Sump always grumbles.
a : All the way. | Every one. | Always.

scene em_dp_rm_glass
when topic=caravan kind=left region=ridgemere
a : Glass from the glassworks went to {other} packed in straw and prayers. | Rope from the Ropewalk's off to {other}. Miles of it. | Mossgrave wool to {other}, three wagons' worth.
b : Prayers break too. | Enough rope to hang the Council. | The roads will smell of sheep for a week.
a : Fewer than glass. | Don't say that out loud. | Longer.

scene em_dp_sf_wine
when topic=caravan kind=left region=ridgemere
a : Rainwater Brewery ale for {other}. They'll drink it before it arrives. | The City Office sealed every crate before the caravan to {other} went. | Wagons out the gate to {other}, Greatly flags flying.
b : The carters will, anyway. | City seals and city tolls. | Greatly does love its flags.
a : Every night. | Always. | Loves itself more.
